WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.470
- You know, they did it again.

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.790
I mean, I actually think that perhaps

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.907
the second season is
stronger than the first.

00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:08.620
(upbeat bass guitar music)

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.540
When I first got the script,
I threw it in the bin.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:12.910
Which is true.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:14.970
I read some of it and I thought,

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.750
this is too broad for me.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.270
And then, my boyfriend who's a writer,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.060
read it and said, you have to do this.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.728
It's so funny, just read it again,

00:00:26.728 --> 00:00:29.590
read it again, read it again.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.680
And I did, and I couldn't put it down.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.513
Maybe I was in a bad mood, (she laughs)

00:00:32.513 --> 00:00:34.640
I don't know what it was.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.090
You know, it was clear in the first season

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:41.240
how bold and brave the writers are.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.300
There are so many predictable ways

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.670
that the storylines could go,

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:51.670
and gratefully, consistently,
pleasantly surprised.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.350
I definitely feel like
a proud mum sometimes

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.320
when observing

00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:00.500
Asa and Ncuti.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.500
I'm constantly surprised how
mature their choices are.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.610
When you're talking about acting,

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.610
and certainly, their teenage
years are closer to hand

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.290
than they are for me, for instance,

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.480
where I can barely remember

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.670
whether I even had a sex ed class or,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.540
who my first snog was.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.420
It is interesting that they are so able

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.700
to give themselves permission, I guess,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.730
to go back and to re-experience

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.790
some of the horrendous
and tumultuous aspects

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.390
of their teenage years.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.680
And I remember thinking that

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.260
when I was watching the first season

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.760
and watching Asa's work and thinking,

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.330
you know, he's really properly good,

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:51.370
there's nothing predictable
in his responses to things.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.580
Jean and Otis, from the very beginning,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:58.220
felt like the least complicated
and difficult element of it.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.160
We immediately fell into a rhythm

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:05.350
and a tone, it just felt very natural

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.610
and effortless from the beginning.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.480
Yeah, they're all properly good.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.570
As an ancient adult, it was hard for me

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:19.570
to really discern what
that reaction was gonna be.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.930
And I've been shocked before by successes

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.500
of things that I've done.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:28.110
Mostly in the opposite
direction! (she laughs)

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.110
But it was hard for me to
judge whether it would be got.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.010
Whether people would get it.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:38.700
Whether the fact that
it was both seemingly

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.100
British and American,
that is was in the past

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.930
and in the present, and
sometimes even in the future.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.620
Well, there's certainly a sense

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.920
when going into a second season,

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:53.920
knowing that a fan base has
properly enjoyed something.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:59.290
That one can imagine what
the reaction might be

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.430
to certain things that happen.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.850
And you know even in the reading of it,

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.130
when you're sitting round the table read

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.360
and when you're reading
it for the first time,

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.230
you think, oh my God,
they're gonna love this!

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.410
Or whatever, and then
so in the doing of it,

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.920
it's a lot of fun to be
able to play with that

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.320
and to stretch it to its extremes.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.690
Knowing that you're held in that place

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:24.370
by a sense of love and appreciation.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:29.370
I think a show like this
is extraordinarily helpful

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.860
in different countries,
in different cultures,

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:35.810
in different neighborhoods
even, in different religions,

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.100
in different emotional relationships.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.560
One of the extraordinary things

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.720
that the show does is it
shows that whoever you are,

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:49.520
and whatever your feelings
or thoughts or proclivities,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.480
or taste or sexual preference,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.810
whoever you claim you are

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.990
and what feels comfortable is okay.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:57.930
So the fact that there's a place

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:02.930
where there is such diverse representation

00:04:03.084 --> 00:04:06.490
and that there is, even
though there is conflict

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.220
and there is pain and there is fear

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.200
and there is lack of communication,

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.320
that somehow that's part of the story,

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.790
that is basically deals with everything.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:19.790
To show youngsters that
everybody goes through that.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:24.710
Everybody around the
world, to some degree,

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.410
will go through the same feelings

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.930
and the same struggles
and the same confusion

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.930
and the same fear, and the same shame

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:32.910
and the same guilt.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.220
And to see, to watch,
and to feel represented

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:39.200
and to feel recognized and heard,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.080
and to feel that you're not alone,

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.950
I think is one of the most valuable things

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.973
anyone can give anybody else.

00:04:47.973 --> 00:04:51.473
(upbeat electronic music)

